Author: JimmyShi22 <417711026@qq.com>
Date:   Sat Nov 14 06:37:31 2026 +0800

    Register the encoded table instance and reuse it by public identity
    
    The anchor command accepts the saved private table randomness, rebuilds the
    same encoded-table commitment the commit published, and prints the public
    instance identity: the anchor leaf count and, per table, the identity,
    configuration, root and record digest. A model with trusted tables and no
    saved material is rejected, and a model without trusted tables rejects
    unexpected material. The matrix accepts a registered commit per case and
    reuses it for every run, so a registered instance is exercised by reruns while
    the new-commit cost is measured by the separate provisioning run. The context
    test reads the registered instance artifacts from the registration archive
    and keeps the old-version artifact rejection under a version-one policy.
    
    The policy registration of the provisioned instances is the next commit.

